{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An entity is one thing in your game or simulation. It has no data of its own: a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores the components it holds, and the handle is how you refer to it. You get a handle by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spawning an entity, and you pass it back to the world to read and change its components:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let hero = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Ada\"), Health(current: 100))","","print(world[Name.self, of: hero].value)","\/\/ Prints \"Ada\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle is a small value, cheap to copy and store, for example in a component that refers to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another entity. It holds two numbers: the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of the slot the entity occupies in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"world, and the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of that slot. When an entity is despawned, the world can reuse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its slot for a new entity with the next generation, so a handle kept past its entity’s despawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"stale"}]},{"type":"text","text":": it never names the entity that took the slot."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","let first = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","world.despawn(first)","let second = world.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 1))","","print(first, second)","\/\/ Prints \"0:0 0:1\"","print(world.contains(first))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities are ordered by slot, then by generation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/_(_:_:)"],"title":"Operators","anchor":"Operators"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/init(index:generation:)"],"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/generation","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/index"],"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/Comparable-Implementations","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity\/Equatable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Entity"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Entity.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/En